`CreateBooking::demo()` breaks the `adapters-main` rule. The command file now imports `InMemoryBookingRepository` and `SequentialIds` at lines 7–10, and `demo()` builds both at lines 56–59. The rule says commands hold ports as `Rc<dyn Port>` and are handed the adapter, and that only `main.rs` and tests construct in-memory or file adapters. The change also moves those imports out of the test module and into production code. A command that picks its own adapters is coupled to them, and the demo tables and seat counts become booking data held in the command layer.

I didn't search for callers of `demo()`. The finding rests on the code in the changed file alone.

